{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097169-jack-the-ripper-and-serial-killers","id":1097169,"title":"Jack the Ripper and Serial Killers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T09:50:54-07:00","id":1097169,"title":"Jack the Ripper and Serial Killers","content":"So. i know that the Vampire Victorian Age mentions different potential views on Jack. but i was wondering if you guys used him on any other game such as a nightmare on changeling, a cult of euthanatoi and so on...<br /> same with other famous serial killers (i had albert fish on a game a la Black House)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:51:51-07:00","id":1097336,"title":"","content":"I think if I was running a Victorian Hunter (as in Society of Leopold/Twilight Agents/Arcanum) game, I'd have him turn out to be an alien organ harvester. <br /> <br /> If you take Alan Moore and Eddie Campbell's graphic novel <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/From_Hell\" target=\"_blank\">From Hell</a> as a starting place, the entire thing can be some sort of deeply weird hermetic or thaumaturgic ritual. <br /> <br /> To be honest, most real life serial killers just aren't that interesting. A <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_serial_killers_by_number_of_victims\" target=\"_blank\">huge majority</a> of them are basically serial rapists who happen to murder their victims for one reason or another. The only ones you can really do much with are the ones who were never caught or identified, like the Zodiac Killer or the Cleveland Torso Murderer, just because no one knows who they were or why they did it. <br /> I, personally, find movie style Slasher killers more workable in the WoD. At least for story purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T17:59:31-07:00","id":1097376,"title":"","content":"Any time a serial killer was used in the games I've played in, it usually ended up being a Gorehound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:32:20-07:00","id":1097532,"title":"","content":"I forget, wasn't there some sort of merit for Kinfolk that allowed them to have a dot or two of Rage? I remember comments by Ethan Skemp back in the day about how even just a single dot of Rage represented a level of primordial fury and anger that your average person has never come anywhere close to experiencing, even on their worst days. So, I'm pondering the concept of a Kinfolk with a single dot of Rage that's this cinematic style killer motivated by ecological fanaticism and some garbled interpretation of Garou philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:11:12-07:00","id":1097546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097169-jack-the-ripper-and-serial-killers?p=1097532#post1097532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, wasn't there some sort of merit for Kinfolk that allowed them to have a dot or two of Rage? I remember comments by Ethan Skemp back in the day about how even just a single dot of Rage represented a level of primordial fury and anger that your average person has never come anywhere close to experiencing, even on their worst days. So, I'm pondering the concept of a Kinfolk with a single dot of Rage that's this cinematic style killer motivated by ecological fanaticism and some garbled interpretation of Garou philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Rage, Gnosis. Kinfolk don't get Rage unless they've been possessed or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:29:14-07:00","id":1097553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097169-jack-the-ripper-and-serial-killers?p=1097546#post1097546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Rage, Gnosis. Kinfolk don't get Rage unless they've been possessed or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yes, that was it. <br /> <br /> Too bad. Seems like an oversight, given all the horror potential for such a thing. <br /> <br /> But then I've spent the past decade or so using Kinfolk+ who sometimes come in Wolf-Blooded or Moon-Touched varieties where such a thing is possible, so that solves my problem already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T08:17:52-07:00","id":1098437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097169-jack-the-ripper-and-serial-killers?p=1097532#post1097532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, wasn't there some sort of merit for Kinfolk that allowed them to have a dot or two of Rage? I remember comments by Ethan Skemp back in the day about how even just a single dot of Rage represented a level of primordial fury and anger that your average person has never come anywhere close to experiencing, even on their worst days. So, I'm pondering the concept of a Kinfolk with a single dot of Rage that's this cinematic style killer motivated by ecological fanaticism and some garbled interpretation of Garou philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the prototype of the Jigsaw style Gorehounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:25:22-07:00","id":1098468,"title":"","content":"Well, the serial killers that we know of tend to be serial rapists with strange fetishistic behaviors like collecting their victims' heads. If you had someone who was addicted to killing who did not engage in rape and/or strange fetishist behaviors, their actions would probably be classified as normal homicides. A smart serial killer of that sort who selected their victims from disadvantaged populations and moved regularly could probably escape capture for decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T21:00:48-07:00","id":1142023,"title":"","content":"Lots of Vampires would effectively be serial killers, especially as humanity drops; but specifically the Nagaraja (who have to consume the Blood rich organs to feed) are serial killers just to exist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T20:17:33-07:00","id":1142394,"title":"","content":"Maybe a silver Fang kinfolk, trying to drive degenerate behaviour off the streets?<br /> <br /> ok ok... I go for &quot;sympathy for the devil&quot; But Jack didnt fit that.<br /> <br /> He didnt just intimidate illicit women, or rough them up ... didnt just kill them a lot of storys Ive heard he posed them...<br /> <br /> think he'd work as a spectre?<br /> <br /> thinking Mortwight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T09:33:37-07:00","id":1142563,"title":"","content":"&quot;He&quot; (She? They?) is alleged to have killed five women (Mary Ann Nichols, Annie Chapman, Elizabeth Stride, Catherine Eddowes, Mary Kelly) over a period of three months by cutting their throats, and with four of them removing one or more internal organs from the abdominal cavity, and the last one (Mary Kelly) being further mutilated. There may have been a possible sixth victim (Alice McKenzie) seven months later, but there has always been a great deal of debate if it was the same killer or a copy cat. <br /> <br /> One of the ironies is that the media frenzy over the murders drew greater attention to the living conditions of the poor in Whitechapel, leading to demands for social reform and several acts of Parliament to help clean up London's slums. With that in mind, one could always posit that the killer was a Child of Gaia trying to bring about that very outcome. For &quot;The Greater Good&quot;, of course.<br /> <br /> Kim Newman's Anno Dracula novel presents the murders as the work of Dr. John Seward, one of Van Helsing's group in the original Dracula, having become a mentally unstable vampire hunter in the wake of Dracula's vampire domination of Britain. <br /> <br /> There's an episode of the original Star Trek series written by Robert Bloch (of Psycho fame), in which the killer is a disembodied energy being that has committed murders on hundreds of worlds over the centuries. <br /> <br /> The Freedom City setting for Green Ronin's Mutants &amp; Masterminds system presents the idea of a &quot;murder spirit&quot; called Jack O'Knives who has been responsible for a number of serial murders around the world as different times, including the Whitechapel murders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}